## Architecture

Three layers, one engine, two frontends.

    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │             mizan_zarb_core                  │
    │  (MIT, public — the engine)                  │
    │  money, models, validation, storage,         │
    │  formulas, reports, analytics, importers     │
    │  No print. No input. No UI. No I/O in APIs. │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                         ▲
                         │ imports
            ┌────────────┴───────────────┐
            │                            │
    ┌───────┴───────┐          ┌─────────┴──────────┐
    │  mizan_zarb   │          │ mizan_zarb_studio  │
    │  CLI (MIT)    │          │ (proprietary GUI)  │
    │  Free forever │          │ Paid, one-time     │
    └───────────────┘          └────────────────────┘

**The engine is the product.** The CLI and GUI are consumers of it.
Anyone can import `mizan_zarb_core` and build their own frontend. This
is what makes the project a platform, not just a tool.

### Non-negotiable boundaries

`mizan_zarb_core` may NOT:
- `print()`
- `input()`
- `sys.exit()`
- Touch ANSI colors, tables, or terminal width
- Know what a menu is
- Import from `mizan_zarb` or `mizan_zarb_studio`

`mizan_zarb` may NOT:
- Contain any business formula (no `mrr = sum(...)`)
- Import from `mizan_zarb_studio`

`mizan_zarb_studio` may NOT:
- Contain any business formula
- Import from `mizan_zarb`

If you can delete the CLI folder and `core` still passes all tests,
the boundary is clean.

