## The Rules (never break)

1. Money is `Decimal`, never `float`. Ever.
2. Zero runtime dependencies in the engine. Ever.
3. No `print()`, `input()`, or `sys.exit()` in `mizan_zarb_core`.
4. Every function has type hints. `mypy --strict` passes.
5. Every formula has tests.
6. Business logic never leaks into the CLI or the GUI.
7. The public API of `mizan_zarb_core` is a contract. Breaking it
   requires a major version bump.
8. The CLI stays free forever. No upsells inside it. The GUI is the
   paid product.
9. MIT license stays MIT. Do not relicense the open core.
10. Local-first means local-first. No cloud backend. No telemetry
    without explicit opt-in. Your data is a file you own.

