## Build Order (core engine)

    1. errors.py           ← exception hierarchy
    2. money.py            ← Decimal primitives, formatting, safe math
    3. models.py           ← dataclasses for all entities
    4. __init__.py         ← public API surface
    5. validation.py       ← email, date, ISO, enum validators
    6. storage/            ← json_store, atomic, paths, backup, migrations
    7. config/             ← schema, defaults, loader
    8. fees/               ← one module per platform
    9. currency/           ← FX engine
    10. formulas/          ← revenue, churn, unit_econ, margins, survival, goals
    11. analytics/         ← cohort, concentration, forecast, anomaly, effective_rate
    12. reports/           ← one module per report
    13. tax/               ← rules, quarterly, vat, deductible
    14. budget/            ← limits, variance, alerts
    15. recurring/         ← normalize, project, detect
    16. notifications/     ← rules, triggers, events
    17. webhooks/          ← dispatcher, payloads
    18. plugins/           ← registry, hooks, api
    19. api/               ← local HTTP server for GUI
    20. search/            ← index, query
    21. tags/              ← cross-cutting labels
    22. audit/             ← append-only change log
    23. importers/         ← stripe, paddle, gumroad, appstore, generic
    24. exporters/         ← csv, json, pdf, accountant
    25. invoicing/         ← generator, numbering, branding
    26. time_tracking/     ← hours, effective_rate
    27. sandbox/           ← demo_data, reset
    28. sync/              ← orchestrator, conflict, state

Then the CLI, then the GUI.

